 "status": "active",
 "title": "Acquisition checks B1-B8 and the per-sign B6b gates (as-measured scan)",
 "description": "Supported-input matrix (B1: LabSpec as8, Trek-type as7, FieldSpec 3 legacy reflectance; per-file detector joins) and the bad-scan checks on the AS-MEASURED reflectance (PLAN v3.2 Step 1-2). Unusable (B1-B4) replaces every verdict with Rescan. B6 is a Check only, raised per model when noise could carry the reading across a verdict cut (DECISIONS 109); never Unusable. B6b gates each contaminant sign (and C1) on the noise of its own statistic: read as measured, or through a near-uncorrected correction (every statistic the noise policies read keeps its noise within 15% of the uncorrected noise; every noise policy then treats the stream exactly like a native standard-resolution scan), today's standard-resolution table on N2; through any other correction, the statistic's noise SD propagated through that correction against a cut fixed once in SD units (DECISIONS 137). N2 is the canonical noise measure (1e-5 absorbance).",
 "licence": "CC-BY-4.0",
 "created": "2026-10-03",
 "provenance": {
  "basis": "SPYDER Bone planning reports 03 (reader), 07 (warnings), Phase 0a A1-A2 (canonical N2, B6b cut 60, correlated-noise gains). B8 thresholds from the relative splice steps of every file in hand (standard-resolution files <= 1.7%, high-resolution sessions <= 6.8%).",
  "per_sign_gates": "Phase 0c (high-resolution noise study): clean false alarms of each sign on 1,201 clean standard-resolution scans with high-resolution-like noise injected, after the v0.2 transfer, as a function of the noise in the sign's own window; cut = the largest N2 at which the false-alarm rate stays within +0.25 points of the noiseless rate (model noise shape; measured shape as the pessimistic bound): wax 80 / 59 -> 60, ester 306 / 215 -> 250, plaster 174 / 125 -> 150, C1 125 / 50 -> 125. Burnt (visible-range edge and short-wave OH bands) is ungated on v0.2; the uncorrected table keeps the shipped gate so standard-resolution behaviour is unchanged.",
  "any_correction": "DECISIONS 137 (g2, 2026-10-19): each sign statistic is linear in absorbance, so its noise SD per unit of measured N2 comes from any blur + absorbance-gain correction by the engine's own propagation (the method of the band and model noise gains; Monte Carlo through v0.2 agrees within 3%). One rule reproduces both shipped tables: gate when the propagated SD exceeds c_s, c_s = the v0.2 gain x the v0.2 cut (plaster 150, wax 60, ester 250, C1 125 on their windows; fallbacks 30 on N2(1500-1600)). On the high-resolution sets in hand it reproduces every v0.2 gate and fallback exactly; the standard-resolution plaster and C1 cuts are the same rule within 1-2%. Kept for streams read as measured (and near-uncorrected corrections, which every noise policy treats as a native standard-resolution scan; Matt, 2026-10-19: standard-res never changes): the shipped table, exactly (LabSpec 4 standard never changes; unifying it would move ester on ~0.3% of standard-resolution scans).",
  "fallbacks": "2026-10-13 (pre-registered): the gates' cut N2(1500-1600) <= 30 (both fallbacks) is the largest noise at which the reduced statistics keep clean false alarms within the noiseless rate on 1,201 clean standard-resolution scans with high-resolution-like noise injected after the v0.2 transfer; 38 of 40 dark high-resolution scans pass it. Not N2(1400-1500) for plaster: the gypsum bands themselves raise it (median 17 -> 46-81 with plaster added), so that gate would close exactly when plaster is present (amendment 1). Since 5.0.0 (DECISIONS 137) the trigger is the reduced statistic's propagated SD at most c (c = the v0.2 gain x 30), the same cut for any correction."
 },
