    "note": "sd_above / sd_at_most = the statistic term's noise gain through this correction (spyder_ref.gains.stat_term_gain, correlation 1.25 nm) x its shipped N2 cut: the cuts are fixed once here, in SD units, and apply to every correction"
   },
   "note": "A sign is gated (not checked) by the noise of its own statistic on the AS-MEASURED scan. Read as measured, or through a near-uncorrected correction: every statistic the noise policies read (the B6b gate and fallback statistics, check.longwave's tail reading, check.signs' soft-tier statistic) has a noise gain within check.acquisition's std_like_within (15%) of its gain as measured, e.g. a standard-resolution unit's own file (every noise policy then treats the stream exactly like a native standard-resolution scan: this table, long-wave not assessed, the soft tier always eligible, the profiles' non_native models and second opinion off): the 'uncorrected' table (gated when N2 of the sign's window exceeds n2_above; no fallbacks). Through any other correction: gated when SD = the statistic's gain in the detector segment holding its N2 window (propagated through the correction) x that N2 exceeds sd_above; a null gate is never gated (burnt: it reads the visible edge, not the noisy SWIR2). A gated sign with a fallback runs its reduced variant instead when the reduced statistic's SD is at most sd_at_most (plaster: the 1446 nm band alone, check.signs plaster.reduced_1446; C1: the variant below 1800 nm, check.c1 swir1); it then counts as checked. A window the scan does not cover: the sign is not checked, 'not available on this instrument'. statistics: sum over windows of weight x mean E over [lo, hi] nm, E from the named kernel (offsets do not matter for noise). The record keeps check.B6b as a summary: n2 = N2(n2_window_nm), signs_gated = the contaminant signs gated with no fallback available (not checked), signs_reduced = the gated signs whose reduced variant is eligible (it runs, except C1 when a specific sign fired: C1 is then skipped as usual), gated = every contaminant sign in signs_gated, outcome Note when either list is non-empty."
  },
